'''White Cyclone''' (ホワイトサイクロン, ''Howaito Saikuron'', '''White Cyclone''') is a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] that appears in [[Special Events|Event Stages]] and [[Zero Legends]]. It was added in [[Version 2.2 Update#Version 2.2.3 Update|Version 2.2.3]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = White Cyclone
|image = E 069.png
|first appearance = [[Attack on W-Cyclone (Expert)|Peerless]]<br>
'''ZL''': [[The Theory of Felinity|Sub-chapter 2 - The Theory of Felinity]]
|money drop = 3,000¢ - 11,850¢
}}

==Enemy==
Unlike the [[Red Cyclone|Red]] and [[Dark Cyclone|Dark]] [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s, this enemy has only one trait: [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], making it slightly more difficult to counter. It has all the trademarks of the Cyclones, with extremely high health and attack power, very low range with somewhat low movement speed, but a lightning fast attack rate and attack animation. Unlike some other Cyclones, however, White Cyclone has a forgiving 5 knockbacks.

Remember that White Cyclone isn't a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy, so don't expect most of the [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] exclusives' abilities to work against it. Fortunately, they can still help against the Traitless support enemies that appear in most of its stages.

==Strategy==
[[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Anti-Floating units]] like [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Bishop Cat]], [[Bodhisattva Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bodhisattva Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Shaman Cat]] and [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fortune Teller Cat]] help a lot, though White Cyclone is backed up by [[THE SLOTH]] in [[Attack on W-Cyclone (Expert)|Attack on W-Cyclone]] and [[Wrath of W-Cyclone (Insane)|Wrath of W-Cyclone]], making it riskier to rely on knockback rather than freeze/slow.

